// EXPECT: [E100]
// ★ `effects write` IS AN ASSERTION OF NOTHING, so it is no longer sayable.
//
// The effect means "writes mutable GLOBAL state", and Lain has none: a top-level `var` is
// [E100], so the bound's domain is EMPTY by language design. Declaring it was therefore always
// satisfied — and W130 would then advise, in the same breath, downgrading the function to
// `func` because it has no observable effect.
//
// That is precisely what law L3 refuses: a spelling that carries no information. The effect
// audit said so three months before this test existed, and `write` stayed sayable because
// nothing rejects a bound that is merely vacuous — it passes every check by construction.
//
// The diagnostic names the two real things a programmer might have meant: mutating through a
// `var` PARAMETER (which is in the signature, and whose write footprint is tracked by a
// separate live mechanism) or doing IO (`effects io`).
proc f(var x i32) effects write {
    x = 1
}
proc main() i32 { return 0 }
